scharge-generation steps instead of one aggregate precursor-forming reaction.", "Correct rxn_002 by adding H2O as product.", "Correct rxn_003 to consume 2 H2O and release NH3.", "Relabel the discharge step as an atmospheric or plasma-aqueous environment rather than generic Surface."]}, {"pathway_id": "P2", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_002": 0.56, "rxn_003": 0.52}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.58, "pathway_coherence": 0.78, "environmental_progression": 0.67, "target_achievement": 0.76, "overall_confidence": 0.63, "feedback": "Among the encoded pathways, this is the cleanest. Strecker capture of isobutyraldehyde to valine aminonitrile and subsequent hydrolysis are textbook chemistry and strongly literature-aligned. But rxn_002 is missing H2O as product, and rxn_003 should be valine aminonitrile + 2 H2O -> valine + NH3. The pathway is still only a final-stage route unless a realistic source of isobutyraldehyde is added elsewhere.", "approved": false, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_002", "rxn_003"], "suggestions": ["Add H2O as product in rxn_002.", "Rewrite rxn_003 as valine aminonitrile + 2 H2O -> valine + NH3.", "Specify aqueous hydrolysis conditions such as pH and temperature.", "Repair mol_008 structure metadata so the aminonitrile node is machine-readable."]}, {"pathway_id": "P3", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_004": 0.62}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.63, "pathway_coherence": 0.82, "environmental_progression": 0.43, "target_achievement": 0.8, "overall_confidence": 0.59, "feedback": "This is directly aligned with Kaur et al. 2024 in reaction class and target. rxn_004 is unbalanced; the correct net is alpha-ketoisovalerate + NH3 + H2 -> valine + H2O. The chemistry is strong as a final step, but the label Biochemical does not match a heterogeneous Ni catalyst system, and upstream alpha-ketoisovalerate synthesis is not provided.", "approved": false, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_004"], "suggestions": ["Add H2O as product in rxn_004.", "Relabel the environment to aqueous mineral-cata