n_009 to use 2 H2O\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.37,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.84\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.44,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.46,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.58,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.82,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.49,\n      \"feedback\": \"The endpoint is literature-consistent only at a very coarse level: acetone plus cyanide/ammonia chemistry can yield valine, but the explicit formaldehyde-assisted C1-extension in rxn_010 is speculative. Friedmann and Miller established the product under NH4CN plus ketone conditions, not this mechanistically explicit sequence. rxn_003 again needs 2 H2O.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_010\",\n        \"rxn_003\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Either collapse this to a documented NH4CN plus acetone overall route or provide isotope-based justification for the formaldehyde C1-extension hypothesis\",\n        \"Correct rxn_003 stoichiometry\",\n        \"State the pH and concentration regime needed for cyanide-ketone chemistry\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.42\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.46,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.40,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.36,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.70,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.45,\n      \"feedback\": \"Fox-Windsor-type heated formaldehyde-ammonia chemistry is a real historical valine report, but the network overstates it as a direct one-step synthesis of free valine. The literature indicates harsh heating, complex hydrolysable precursor material, poor mechanistic resolution, and weak modern reproducibility for valine specifically.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_011\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Repre